{"name":"Butter Fingers","hex":"#fce9ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butter fingers","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of butterfingers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter_fingers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butterfinger","blocks":[{"text":"Butterfinger is a candy bar manufactured by US-based Ferrara Candy Company, a subsidiary of Ferrero. It was formerly manufactured internationally by Nestlé. It consists of a layered crisp peanut butter core covered in a chocolate-like coating; the coating is not eligible to be described as chocolate, as it contains no cocoa butter. Butterfinger was invented by Otto Schnering of the Curtiss Candy Company in 1923. A popularity contest chose the name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfinger"},{"title":"Butterfinger (Canadian band)","blocks":[{"text":"Butterfinger was a Saskatchewan-based Canadian alternative rock band which released one independently recorded studio album."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterfinger_(Canadian_band)"},{"title":"Butter Fingers","blocks":[{"text":"Butter Fingers is a 1925 American silent film sports comedy film directed by Del Lord starring Billy Bevan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Butter_Fingers_%281925%29_-_1.jpg/330px-Butter_Fingers_%281925%29_-_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter_Fingers"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.